{title: God Will Take Care of You}
{artist: Fanny Crosby / Ira D. Sankey}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: C}
{key_original: Db}
{tempo: 115}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Photocopied score; origin unknown. Paired with words to Fanny Crosby\'s \"God Will Take Care of You.\" Publication date found at http://www.hymnary.org)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C7]God will take care of you, be not [F]af[C]raid;
[Em]He [G7]is your safeguard through sunshine and [C]shade;
[C]Tenderly watching and keeping His [F]own,
[F]He will not [C]leave you to wan[G7]der a[C]lone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G7]God will take [C]care of you [G7]still to the [Am]end;
[F]Oh, what a [C]Father, Re[D7]deemer, and [G]friend!
[C]Jesus will answer whenever you call;
[Dm]He [F]will take [C]care of you, [Am]trust Him [G7]for [C]all.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C7]God will take care of you, through all [F]the [C]day,
[Em]Shiel[G7]ding your footsteps, directing your [C]way;
[C]He is your shepherd, protector, and [F]guide,
[F]Leading His [C]children where still [G7]waters [C]glide.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C7]God will take care of you long as [F]you [C]live,
[Em]Gran[G7]ting you blessings no other can [C]give;
[C]He will take care of you when time is [F]past,
[F]Safe to His [C]kingdom will bring [G7]you at [C]last.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
